(CAR BOOKING APPLICATION SECURITY REMEDIATION REPORT) Tj
T*
(===================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Course: SE4030 – Secure Software Development) Tj
T*
(Application: Car Booking Portal \(PHP/MySQL\)) Tj
T*
(Team: _Update with final member names and index numbers_) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Executive Summary) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A baseline security review of the legacy car booking portal uncovered multiple high-risk) Tj
T*
(defects across authentication, session handling, and booking workflows. Attackers could bypass) Tj
T*
(authentication via SQL injection, capture credentials hashed with obsolete MD5, hijack active) Tj
T*
(sessions, and plant persistent cross-site scripting \(XSS\) payloads. The team refactored the) Tj
T*
(application to enforce prepared statements, modern password hashing, CSRF protection, secure) Tj
T*
(session cookies, robust input validation, and systematic output escaping. Google OAuth 2.0) Tj
T*
(single sign-on now supplements local accounts, reducing password surface area. The hardened) Tj
T*
(build closes seven critical gaps, adds observability around database failures, and documents) Tj
T*
(deployment steps so the fixes remain effective in production.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Application Overview) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The portal allows customers to browse available vehicles, submit booking requests, and manage) Tj
T*
(reservations, while an administrator back-office confirms bookings and maintains the inventory.) Tj
T*
(The stack is pure PHP with a MySQL database and server-side rendered views. Authentication) Tj
T*
(originally relied on custom forms without any framework support, leaving input handling and) Tj
T*
(session security bespoke and error-prone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Assessment Methodology) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The team combined manual code review with targeted dynamic checks to enumerate vulnerabilities) Tj
T*
(and confirm fixes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reviewed historical commits and key entry points \(login.php, register.php, carDetails.php,) Tj
T*
(  admin panel\) to locate insecure database usage, validation gaps, and missing defenses.) Tj
T*
(- Exercised forms with Burp Suite Community Edition and browser developer tools to replicate) Tj
T*
(  SQL injection, CSRF, and XSS issues.) Tj
T*
(- Applied PHPStan level 1, PHP’s native php -l syntax checks, and MySQL error logs to verify) Tj
T*
(  refactors and guardrails after each remediation.) Tj
T*
(- Re-tested exploitation attempts post-fix to ensure mitigations block the original payloads) Tj
T*
(  without regressing functionality.) Tj
ET
endstream

endobj
