stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
72 742 Td
(V-03: Missing CSRF Protection on Key Forms) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Category: Cross-Site Request Forgery) Tj
T*
(- Original risk: Login, registration, and booking forms accepted POST requests without CSRF) Tj
T*
(  tokens, permitting attackers to force authenticated victims to perform sensitive actions.) Tj
T*
(- Remediation: Added a reusable helper \(inc/security.php\) that issues per-session CSRF tokens) Tj
T*
(  and validates them on submission. Tokens now guard customer, admin, and booking flows.) Tj
T*
(- Validation: Confirmed that replaying a stored POST without the token is rejected with an) Tj
T*
(  “Invalid session” error and no state change occurs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(V-04: Insecure Session Cookies and Session Fixation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Category: Session Management) Tj
T*
(- Original risk: PHP sessions used default cookie parameters \(no Secure, HttpOnly, or SameSite) Tj
T*
(  flags\) and did not regenerate IDs post-login, exposing users to fixation and theft.) Tj
T*
(- Remediation: Centralized session bootstrap configures cookie flags \(Secure, HttpOnly,) Tj
T*
(  SameSite=Strict\) and regenerates the session identifier after both user and admin) Tj
T*
(  authentication. Logout clears the session to invalidate stolen IDs.) Tj
T*
(- Validation: Browser developer tools confirm the hardened flags, and repeated login attempts) Tj
T*
(  issue fresh session identifiers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(V-05: Stored and Reflected XSS via Unescaped Output) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Category: Cross-Site Scripting) Tj
T*
(- Original risk: Views such as carDetails.php, cars.php, my_account.php, and admin dashboards) Tj
T*
(  echoed database fields without escaping. Any HTML injected into vehicle titles,) Tj
T*
(  descriptions, or booking messages executed in other users’ browsers.) Tj
T*
(- Remediation: Introduced an escape\(\) helper to perform HTML encoding and applied it to every) Tj
T*
(  dynamic rendering path, including image paths and status labels.) Tj
T*
(- Validation: Injected <script> payloads now render harmlessly as text, and content security) Tj
T*
(  review confirmed no remaining raw echoes in updated templates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(V-06: Booking Workflow Validation Gaps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Category: Input Validation) Tj
T*
(- Original risk: Booking submissions accepted arbitrary date strings and lengthy HTML in the) Tj
T*
(  message field. Attackers could create impossible reservations or plant malicious markup for) Tj
T*
(  later execution in admin views.) Tj
T*
(- Remediation: Server-side validation now enforces real calendar dates with chronological) Tj
T*
(  ordering, trims and strips markup from messages, and bounds length to 500 characters before) Tj
ET
endstream

endobj
